00:29:33,020 --> 00:29:37,020
 path to the side of things, but something that I've been using for a while

257
00:29:37,020 --> 00:29:41,020
 now that helps a lot when building these types of systems.

258
00:29:41,020 --> 00:29:45,020
 I'm using a system for prompts that's called

259
00:29:45,020 --> 00:29:50,020
 kind of like a framework for prompts. It has five sections.

260
00:29:50,020 --> 00:29:54,020
 And this, what we're seeing on the screen right now, is the change specialist.

261
00:29:54,020 --> 00:29:59,020
 It's shortened to fit on the screen. But it's following these five steps.

262
00:29:59,020 --> 00:30:02,020
 So first off, the role, who the agent is and what it knows.

263
00:30:02,020 --> 00:30:08,020
 Instructions is the actual task for the specialist. It's a sentence or two.

264
00:30:08,020 --> 00:30:14,020
 Steps, those are the steps that it should take to be able to do the work.

265
00:30:14,020 --> 00:30:17,020
 when there's more than one single decision.

266
00:30:17,020 --> 00:30:21,020
 An expectation is exactly what comes back from the agent,

267
00:30:21,020 --> 00:30:25,020
 which is what makes the gate on the previous slide possible.

268
00:30:25,020 --> 00:30:28,020
 And then narrowing, what it must never do.

269
00:30:28,020 --> 00:30:31,020
 Never list options, never change a confirmation number,

270
00:30:31,020 --> 00:30:34,020
 never add details that aren't in the product.

271
00:30:34,020 --> 00:30:38,020
 And this isn't going to make the model deterministic,

272
00:30:38,020 --> 00:30:41,020
 but it makes it deterministic-ish.

273
00:30:41,020 --> 00:30:46,540
 The same kind of message is going to get the same kind of answer most of the time.

